<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null ==> this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the index is within the valid range (0 to the size of the list inclusive), then for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element at this index was null, or equal to the old element at this index. Note that the condition is adjusted to handle the shift in indices after the insertion.
